Telescope alternating cocycle congruences b0 = sum_{j=0}^{N} 2^j a_j modulo 2^(N+1):
N=1: b0 = 1 (mod 4); 3*b0+1 = 0 modulo 4.
N=3: b0 = 5 (mod 16); 3*b0+1 = 0 modulo 16.
N=5: b0 = 21 (mod 64); 3*b0+1 = 0 modulo 64.
N=7: b0 = 85 (mod 256); 3*b0+1 = 0 modulo 256.
N=11: b0 = 1365 (mod 4096); 3*b0+1 = 0 modulo 4096.
N=15: b0 = 21845 (mod 65536); 3*b0+1 = 0 modulo 65536.
These finite congruences individually have solutions. The infinite incompatibility with an integer b0 is proved in F.tex.
